| counts_gene | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper | 02_bioinformatics/rnaseq_bulk/01_nfcore-rnaseq-wrapper/run/results/star_salmon/salmon.merged.gene_counts_length_scaled.tsv |
| design | 01_prepare_samplesheets | 01_samplesheets/rnaseq_bulk_design.csv |

## Method
1. Load the gene counts matrix (TSV) and design file (CSV) using Python with pandas in the gars-bio conda environment.
2. Filter to genes with sufficient counts (mean count ≥ 1 across all samples) to remove low-abundance noise.
3. Apply log2(counts + 1) transformation to normalize the count distribution.
4. Center and scale the gene expression matrix to unit variance.
5. Compute PCA using scikit-learn's decomposition.PCA, retaining all components.
6. Extract PC1 and PC2 scores (which together explain the majority of variance).
7. Generate a scatter plot (matplotlib or seaborn) with samples on axes PC1 vs PC2, colored by condition from the design file.
8. Save the PCA plot as PNG and the PC coordinates (samples × components) as CSV.
9. All steps run on the batch executor in a single Python script.

